#: package/analyses/riverplot.description
#: riverplot/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates comprehensive river plots, alluvial diagrams, and stream charts to "
"visualize\n"
"flows, transitions, and temporal changes in categorical data. Supports "
"individual\n"
"entity tracking, aggregate trends, and multi-stage pathways. Perfect for "
"patient\n"
"journeys, treatment progressions, categorical changes over time, and flow "
"analysis."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/swimmerplot.description
#: swimmerplot/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates comprehensive swimmer plots using the ggswim package to visualize "
"patient timelines, clinical events, milestones, and treatment responses. "
"Features enhanced data validation and complete ggswim integration for "
"professional clinical visualization."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/toxicityprofile.description
msgid ""
"Creates comprehensive visualizations of adverse event profiles showing "
"frequency and severity."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/consortdiagram.description
#: consortdiagram/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates CONSORT 2010 compliant flow diagrams for clinical trials using the "
"consort R package.\n"
"Automatically calculates participant numbers from patient-level data with "
"exclusion columns.\n"
"Follows the approach described by Riinu Ots "
"(https://www.riinu.me/2024/02/consort/)."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/decisiongraph.description
#: decisiongraph/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates decision tree graphs for cost-effectiveness analysis with typical "
"decision nodes, chance nodes, and terminal nodes. Supports visualization of "
"treatment pathways, probabilities, costs, and outcomes."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/economistplots.description
#: economistplots/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates elegant Economist-style distribution plots using ggeconodist package\n"
"for professional publication-quality visualizations. Provides diminutive \n"
"distribution charts that effectively communicate statistical distribution \n"
"characteristics with The Economist's distinctive visual style. Perfect for \n"
"comparing distributions across categories, showing price variations, or \n"
"visualizing any statistical distribution data in clinical research."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/subgroupforest.description
#: subgroupforest/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates forest plots showing treatment effects across different patient "
"subgroups. Performs subgroup analysis for clinical trials and observational "
"studies, calculating treatment effects within patient subgroups and testing "
"for interactions. Supports survival (time-to-event), binary, and continuous "
"outcomes with comprehensive statistical validation and heterogeneity testing."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/groupedbar.description
#: groupedbar/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates grouped bar charts to compare measurements, responses, or outcomes \n"
"across different groups. Suitable for comparing lab values across disease "
"groups,\n"
"treatment responses across hospitals, survey responses across demographics,\n"
"or any metric that varies by categorical groupings."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/groupedforest.description
#: groupedforest/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates grouped hazard regression forest plots to show treatment vs control "
"comparisons\n"
"across different variants or subgroups. This module performs Cox "
"proportional hazards\n"
"regression separately for each subgroup defined by a grouping variable and "
"presents\n"
"the hazard ratios in a single forest plot. Perfect for showing treatment "
"effects\n"
"across patient variants, genetic subtypes, or clinical subgroups."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/pcaloadingheatmap.description
msgid ""
"Creates heatmap and barmap visualizations of PCA loadings for easy "
"interpretation\n"
"of component structure. Heatmaps show all loadings as a color-coded matrix, "
"while\n"
"barmaps display loading patterns as bar charts across components."
msgstr ""

#: pcaloadingheatmap/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates heatmap and barmap visualizations of PCA loadings for easy "
"interpretation\n"
"of component structure. Heatmaps show all loadings as a color-coded matrix, "
"while\n"
"barmaps display loading patterns as bar charts across components.\n"
"\n"
"Both visualizations support optional significance indicators (stars) for "
"loadings\n"
"above a specified cutoff threshold. These publication-ready plots help "
"identify\n"
"which variables contribute most strongly to each component."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/hullplot.description
#: hullplot/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates Hull plots to visualize clusters and groups in scatter plots using "
"ggforce.\n"
"Hull plots draw polygonal boundaries around data points grouped by "
"categorical variables,\n"
"making it easy to identify customer segments, group membership, and data "
"clusters.\n"
"Based on the geom_mark_hull() function from ggforce package."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/linechart.description
#: linechart/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates line charts for time series analysis and trend visualization, with "
"support for multiple groups, confidence intervals, and statistical overlays."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/lollipop.description
#: lollipop/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates lollipop charts for categorical data visualization following R Graph "
"Gallery best practices, with emphasis on clinical applications like patient "
"timelines, treatment outcomes, and biomarker comparisons. Uses "
"geom_segment() and geom_point() for optimal visual presentation."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/tinytable.description
#: tinytable/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates modern, publication-ready tables using the tinytable package.\n"
"This module provides lightweight, zero-dependency table formatting with \n"
"multiple output formats including HTML, LaTeX, PDF, and Word. Designed\n"
"to complement existing ClinicoPath table modules with modern styling,\n"
"flexible formatting, and clean aesthetics. Perfect for enhancing data\n"
"presentation in clinical research publications and reports."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/jjoncoplot.description
#: jjoncoplot/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates oncoplots (mutation landscapes) to visualize genomic alterations "
"across genes and samples with optional clinical annotations."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/bbcplots.description
msgid ""
"Creates professional BBC News-style data visualizations using the bbplot "
"package design principles."
msgstr ""

#: bbcplots/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates professional BBC News-style data visualizations using the bbplot "
"package design principles.\n"
"\n"
"This module implements the BBC Visual and Data Journalism team's design "
"standards for creating\n"
"publication-ready graphics with clean typography, consistent color schemes, "
"and professional\n"
"branding elements. Perfect for creating news-quality visualizations for "
"reports, presentations,\n"
"and publications.\n"
"\n"
"Features BBC's signature minimalist aesthetic with Helvetica typography, "
"strategic use of\n"
"gridlines, and standardized chart dimensions optimized for digital "
"publication."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/coefplot.description
#: coefplot/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates professional coefficient plots (forest plots) for regression models. "
"Visualizes coefficients and confidence intervals from linear, logistic, and  "
"Cox regression models. Supports multiple models comparison, custom "
"coefficient selection, standardized coefficients, and various styling "
"options. Essential  for presenting regression results in clinical research "
"and epidemiological studies."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/studydiagram.description
#: studydiagram/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates professional study flow diagrams including CONSORT diagrams and "
"flowcharts using multiple rendering engines"
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/enhancedtables.description
#: enhancedtables/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates professional, publication-ready tables using the gt package.\n"
"This module provides comprehensive table formatting with advanced styling,\n"
"grouping, summary statistics, and clinical research optimizations. \n"
"Designed for high-quality table presentation in medical publications,\n"
"reports, and presentations. Features include conditional formatting,\n"
"custom themes, statistical summaries, and multi-level grouping."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/ggprism.description
#: ggprism/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates publication-ready plots with GraphPad Prism styling using ggprism "
"package.\n"
"This module provides Prism-style themes, color palettes, and statistical "
"annotations\n"
"to create professional scientific visualizations. Perfect for clinical "
"research \n"
"publications, biostatistics, and academic presentations. Supports various "
"plot \n"
"types including violin plots, box plots, scatter plots, and dose-response "
"curves\n"
"with seamless ggplot2 integration and Prism-style aesthetics."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/raincloud.description
#: raincloud/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Creates Raincloud plots to visualize data distributions using ggdist "
"package.\n"
"Raincloud plots combine three visualization techniques: half-violin plots "
"showing \n"
"distribution density, box plots showing summary statistics, and dot plots "
"showing \n"
"individual data points. This provides a comprehensive view of data "
"distribution \n"
"that reveals patterns traditional box plots might miss, including "
"multimodality\n"
"and distribution shape. Based on the ggdist R-Bloggers tutorial."
msgstr ""

