"diagnostic or prognostic performance. Essential for converting \n"
"continuous measurements to clinically actionable thresholds and \n"
"preventing arbitrary cutpoint selection in pathology studies."
msgstr ""

#: package/analyses/pathsampling.description
msgid ""
"Determines the minimum number of tissue samples (blocks, cassettes, "
"sections, or lymph nodes) required to detect lesions with specified "
"confidence levels. Uses binomial probability models and bootstrap resampling "
"to calculate diagnostic yield curves, sensitivity estimates, and clinical "
"recommendations. Essential for establishing sampling protocols in omentum "
"evaluation, lymph node dissection, and serial sectioning studies. Based on "
"statistical methods from Skala & Hagemann 2015, Gönen et al. 2009, and "
"beta-binomial modeling approaches for pathology sampling research."
msgstr ""

