#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"Every case received the same predicted probability, so the classification "
"metrics below are artefacts of a default 0.500 threshold that assigns "
"everyone to one group: %s. Only the AUC of 0.500 is interpretable."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncombine.b.R
msgid ""
"Every complete case has gold standard \"{level}\", so this sample contains "
"no disease-absent cases. Specificity and NPV cannot be estimated and are "
"reported as blank. Diagnostic accuracy assessment requires both diseased and "
"non-diseased cases."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncombine.b.R
msgid ""
"Every complete case has gold standard \"{level}\", so this sample contains "
"no disease-present cases. Sensitivity and PPV cannot be estimated and are "
"reported as blank. Diagnostic accuracy assessment requires both diseased and "
"non-diseased cases."
msgstr ""

#: R/multisurvival.b.R
msgid ""
"Every one of the %s patients is set to <i>%s</i> = each level in turn%s, a "
"survival curve is predicted for each patient from the fitted model, and "
"those curves are averaged. The procedure repeats for every level."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncombine.b.R
msgid ""
"Every pattern and strategy is reported together with no adjustment for "
"multiple comparisons. Treat the best-looking row as a hypothesis to confirm "
"in new data, not as an established result."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncombine.b.R
msgid ""
"Every row is estimated directly from the observed joint results, not derived "
"from the individual tests' sensitivity and specificity. These figures "
"therefore do not assume the tests are conditionally independent given "
"disease status, and they remain valid when the tests share biology or "
"technology. They do assume this sample's case mix resembles the population "
"the rule would be used in."
msgstr ""

#: R/decisioncombine.b.R
msgid ""
"Every row is estimated directly from the observed joint results, not derived "
"from the individual tests' sensitivity and specificity. These figures "
"therefore do NOT require the tests to be conditionally independent given "
"disease status, and they stay valid when the tests share biology, specimen "
"or technology. That is the main difference from a sequential-testing "
"calculator, which must assume independence and warns about it."
msgstr ""

#: R/multisurvival.b.R
msgid ""
"Every selected explanatory variable is also a stratification variable. A "
"stratified variable is absorbed into the baseline hazard and has no hazard "
"ratio, so no multivariable model can be fitted. Remove at least one variable "
"from the stratification list, or add a covariate that is not stratified."
msgstr ""

#: R/reportcat.b.R
msgid ""
"Every selected variable was empty or all-missing, so there is nothing to "
"summarise."
msgstr ""

#: R/summarydata.b.R
msgid ""
"Every statistic here is computed per row. If the dataset holds several rows "
"per patient (one per block, core or visit), aggregate to one row per patient "
"before reading these numbers as patient-level results."
msgstr ""
"Buradaki her istatistik satır başına hesaplanır. Veri kümesinde hasta başına "
"birden fazla satır varsa (örneğin blok, kor veya ziyaret başına bir satır), "
"bu sayıları hasta düzeyinde yorumlamadan önce verileri hasta başına tek "
"satır olacak şekilde birleştirin."

#: R/tableone.b.R
msgid ""
"Every value of this variable is missing, so it cannot be summarised and does "
"not appear in the table below."
msgstr ""
"Bu değişkenin tüm değerleri eksik olduğundan özetlenemez ve aşağıdaki "
"tabloda yer almaz."

