#: R/lassologistic.b.R
msgid ""
"Predictors were standardized before fitting so that the penalty treats them "
"comparably, but the Coefficient and Odds Ratio columns are reported on the "
"ORIGINAL measurement scale (per 1 unit of a continuous predictor, or present "
"vs absent for a binary one). The Importance column is the "
"per-standard-deviation magnitude, which is what can be compared across "
"predictors with different units. Odds ratios remain penalized (shrunk toward "
"1)."
msgstr ""

#: R/lassocox.b.R
msgid ""
"Predictors were standardized internally within glmnet fitting for the "
"penalty calculation. glmnet back-transforms the displayed coefficients to "
"the original design-column scale; indicator-column hazard ratios therefore "
"compare that category with its reference category. Indicators are still "
"penalized and selected separately rather than as a grouped factor."
msgstr ""
"Ceza hesabı için yordayıcılar glmnet içinde standartlaştırıldı. glmnet "
"gösterilen katsayıları özgün tasarım sütunu ölçeğine geri dönüştürür; "
"gösterge sütunlarının hazard oranları ilgili kategoriyi referans kategoriyle "
"karşılaştırır. Göstergeler yine grup olarak değil ayrı ayrı cezalandırılır "
"ve seçilir."

#: package/analyses/ihcpredict.description
msgid ""
"Predicts diagnoses for cases with unknown diagnoses based on IHC marker "
"expression patterns,\n"
"using a trained reference model from previously analyzed cases with known "
"diagnoses."
msgstr ""

#: ihcpredict/options.description.main
msgid ""
"Predicts diagnoses for cases with unknown diagnoses based on IHC marker "
"expression patterns,\n"
"using a trained reference model from previously analyzed cases with known "
"diagnoses.\n"
"\n"
"**Requirements:**\n"
"- Training dataset analyzed with `ihccluster` (with known diagnoses)\n"
"- Query dataset with same IHC markers (unknown diagnoses to predict)\n"
"- Marker names and data types must match between datasets\n"
"\n"
"**Output:**\n"
"- Predicted diagnosis per case with confidence level\n"
"- Alternative diagnoses (differential)\n"
"- Evidence supporting each prediction\n"
"- Flags for atypical/low-confidence cases"
msgstr ""

