"This selection produces %d variable-by-group combinations (%d variables x %d "
"group levels). Each variable adds rows and one more significance test, so "
"the table becomes long to read and the multiple-testing correction gets more "
"conservative - genuine differences are harder to detect. Consider splitting "
"the variables over two or three separate Cross Table analyses, or grouping "
"rare levels of the grouping variable together."
